== <translate><!--T:7--> Six types of prayer</translate> == 
;<translate><!--T:8-->
Praise</translate>
:<translate><!--T:9-->
Worship God for who He is. (Psalms 34:2)</translate>
;<translate><!--T:10-->
Thanksgiving</translate>
:<translate><!--T:11-->
Thank God for His mercy and providence. (1 Thessalonians 5:18)</translate>
;<translate><!--T:12-->
Lament</translate>
:<translate><!--T:13-->
Cry out your pain and express your complaints to God. (Psalms 13:1-3)</translate>
;<translate><!--T:14-->
Confessing sins</translate>
:<translate><!--T:15-->
Ask God to forgive your sins. (1 John 1:9)</translate>
;<translate><!--T:16-->
Requests</translate>
:<translate><!--T:17-->
Ask God to meet your own needs. (Philippians 4:6-7)</translate>
;<translate><!--T:18-->
Intercession</translate>
:<translate><!--T:19-->
Ask God to meet the needs of others. (1 Timothy 2:1)</translate>
== <translate><!--T:20--> How God’s will affects our prayer</translate> ==
<translate><!--T:68--> There are 3 different types of prayer regarding God’s will:</translate>
<translate><!--T:33--> # God has already made the decision</translate><br/><translate><!--T:34--> Example: “Lord, I want to be born another time and at another place.”</translate><br/>{{Translatable template|Italic|<translate><!--T:35--> → No matter how much you pray, nothing will ever change.</translate>}}
<translate><!--T:36--> # God knows that what we pray for is not really good for us. But because we continue to pray for it and don’t listen to what He actually wants to say to us, He finally says “okay”, hoping that we’ll learn from the consequences.</translate><br/><translate><!--T:37--> Example: A small child comes to his parents and wants to carry the cup of water to the table. The parents know the table is still too high for them and suggests to carry it together with the child. But the child is stubborn: “No! I do it!” Finally the parents agree. But just as they expected, the child drops the cup.<br/>The parents comfort the child, give him dry cloths and wipe away the water. Again they suggest that they carry the cup together. This time the child agrees and all are happy.</translate><br/>{{Translatable template|Italic|<translate><!--T:38--> → Is what you pray for really good? Do you pray with the right motives?</translate>}}<br/>{{Translatable template|Italic|<translate> <!--T:69--> → You have to take the responsibility for the results.</translate>}}
<translate><!--T:39--> # We pray according to God’s will</translate><br/>{{Translatable template|Italic|<translate><!--T:40--> → He will do it! Find out more about God’s will and pray it. (1 John 5:14)</translate>}}
